From 0fb388239b1af590d12aae1a9e34f79c1c576edc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Milad <mmaziesf@uwaterloo.ca>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:56:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Support the M5Stack Core2 v1.1 (AXP2101 PMU)

The Core2 v1.1 replaces the v1.0's AXP192 with an AXP2101 at the same I2C
address but a different register map, so the v1.0 build must not run on it.
Espressif's m5stack_core_2 BSP already handles the v1.1 rails and backlight
(BSP_PMU_AXP2101); this adds AXP2101 branches for the board file's own PMU
access, taken from M5Unified's AXP2101 driver and Core2 v1.1 setup:

- PEK events from IRQ status 1 (0x49, bits 3/2), cleared by write-back
- battery voltage from 0x34-0x35 (14-bit, 1 mV), charge state from 0x01,
  VBUS and battery presence from 0x00, ADCs on via 0x30
- backlight on/off through the BSP (BLDO1), power off via 0x10 bit 0

New build profile core2v11 (devices/sdkconfig.muse-m5stack-core2-v11) in
board.sh, ports.py and avatar.py; the board reports "M5Stack Core2 v1.1" so
avatar.py rebuilds the right profile. The Core2 button test now runs its
scenarios against both PMUs' PEK layouts. Tested on a Core2 v1.1: boots,
display and backlight work, pairs and talks to Muse.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
